  "protocol": "Served-game measurement for the batched-gates change (agents/reference/trading-design.md's post-data note, 'the collector cost gate fails at 2.9-3.6x'): linear2400-c5.onnx (contract 5, seat 0) vs three heximax seats, seeded 4200, driven through hexset.server.api.Tables / hexset.clients.botclient.LocalSearchBrain -- the same Tables.act code path an embedded server bot runs -- for 10 rounds (Game.turns reaching 40). BotRunner's real poll loop (1s default interval, one thread a seat) would drown a millisecond-scale gate-cost change in polling latency, so this drives the same LocalSearchBrain.decide/Tables.act calls synchronously in one thread, back to back, instead of via background poller threads -- still Tables end to end, just without poll-interval noise that would land equally on both arms anyway. 'before' is origin/main at 5596778 (git stash of this PR's diff, same venv, no reinstall needed); 'after' is this PR. Three interleaved before/after trials, same seed each time, on a box whose load rose across the run (loadavg climbed roughly 5 -> 14 over the six runs) -- heximax's own per-turn cost is the control: its ratio should read ~1.0 (noise only), since neither heximax nor search2 override accepts_many.",
